  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1032 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nOn Monday, Middle TN is between the high still to the west and \ntroughing to the east. This allows for a low chance of diurnally-\ndriven storms, primarily across the Plateau. But by Tuesday, the \nhigh works its way back over the southeastern US which keeps \ntemperatures in the 90s through the end of next week. These \ntemperatures don't look like they'll be as hot as this current heat \nwave with heat index values staying below that 105 degree heat\nadvisory criteria. But these above normal readings for September \nwill still be uncomfortable. With the high overhead, it does bring\ndry conditions for at least Tuesday & Wednesday. We'll have to \nlook ahead to next Thursday for the possibility of a pattern shift\nand the return of some low rain chances.",
